/*
FlightsSearch Search flights

Searches flight itineraries and the fares bookable on them.

Send one slice per flight (one for one-way, two for a return, more for a multi-city trip) and every passenger;
at least one passenger must be an `adult`, and children and infants need an `age`. Optional
`filters`: `maxStops`, `preferredAirlines` and `excludedAirlines` select itineraries;
`refundableOnly` and `maxPrice` select fares, and an itinerary left without a fare is not returned.
The body rejects an unknown field at every level, and the route takes no query parameters.
            
Returns `{ items, pagination }`. Each item is one itinerary, the same flights sold by the same airline, with
its fares as `offers`, cheapest first; items are ordered by their cheapest fare, then total duration.
`page` and `limit` (defaults 1 and 10, `limit` at most 100) page through itineraries, and
`pagination.totalCount` counts them. Each page runs a new airline search, so fares can change between pages.
            
An item's `id` is valid only within this response and cannot be ordered; quote and order an offer's
`publicId` before its `details.expiresAt`. Prices are for all passengers, in `currency` or the API
key's currency, and are indicative.
            
Errors: an invalid or unknown field, or a query parameter, 400 / 10001; an unsupported `currency`
404 / 10004. A browser session may not send `filters.maxPrice` (400 / 10001, `NOT_ALLOWED`).

 @param ctx context.Context - for authentication, logging, cancellation, deadlines, tracing, etc. Passed from http.Request or context.Background().
 @return ApiFlightsSearchRequest
*/
